        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "text": "2. Mr. S. S. Chauhan, learned D.A.G. assisted by Mr. Vikash Uniyal, learned Brief Holder for the State.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 296,
      "end": 400,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "S. S. Chauhan",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 304,
          "end": 317
        },
        {
          "text": "Vikash Uniyal",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 350,
          "end": 363
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "3. There are more than 11 matters against the petitioner as observed on 22.08.2025 by this Court,\nwhereby the learned counsel for the petitioner had referred to a judgment \"Ravinder Singh Sidhu vs.\nState of Punjab and others, 2025 SCC Online SC 1164\" that all the matters may be consolidated.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 401,
      "end": 694,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "22.08.2025",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 474,
          "end": 484
        },
        {
          "text": "Ravinder Singh Sidhu vs.\nState of Punjab and others, 2025 SCC Online SC 1164",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 575,
          "end": 651
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 6,
      "text": "4. Learned State counsel, however, had sought time for further instructions and report in the present matter and further makes a submission that unless charge-sheet in all the matters are not submitted, the plea may not be considered.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 696,
      "end": 930,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "He further makes a submission that there is still one case pending being Case Crime No.142 of 2024 under Section 420, 120-B, 467, 468, 471 of IPC and 3, 21(3) of BUDS Act and 3 UPID Act, P.S.\nKotwali Kotdwar, District Pauri Garhwal against the petitioner.\n5. Counter affidavit has been filed on behalf of the State.\n6. Learned counsel for the petitioner seeks and is granted two weeks' time to file rejoinder affidavit.\n7. List this matter on 26.09.2025.\n(Ashish Naithani, J.) 04.09.2025 Akash WPCRL/624/2025 on 4 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/66652897/\n1",
